<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<assembly manifestVersion="1.0" xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">
  <!--
    WHY ELEVATED. The overlay must run at the same integrity level as the League game
    (which runs elevated). Windows UIPI stops a lower-integrity process from receiving
    keyboard input while a higher-integrity window is in the foreground, so without this
    the hotkeys work everywhere EXCEPT in game — which is the only place they matter.

    WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES — corrected 2026-08-21. The earlier text here said this build
    "does not hook input". That stopped being true when hotkeys moved from RegisterHotKey
    (whose WM_HOTKEY messages the focused game swallowed, even elevated) to a
    WH_KEYBOARD_LL hook, and the wording was never updated. Stating it plainly instead:

      * It DOES install a low-level keyboard hook (Hotkeys/LowLevelHotkeyHook.cs).
      * That hook NEVER swallows a key — HookCallback has exactly one return path,
        CallNextHookEx, so every keystroke reaches the game untouched.
      * It NEVER logs, stores, buffers or transmits a keystroke. The only state kept is the
        set of registered hotkey combos plus which modifier keys are currently held.
      * It does NOT use GetAsyncKeyState/GetKeyboardState, and sends NO input
        (no SendInput/keybd_event) — it cannot act on the player's behalf (P4).
      * It does NOT read game memory or inject code into any process (P3).

    In effect it is RegisterHotKey that also works over the game. If you would rather not
    run a build that installs a keyboard hook at all, the alternative implementation
    (Hotkeys/Win32HotkeyHook.cs) is still in the tree — but it loses in-game hotkeys and
    the click-to-target modifier gate that depends on IsModifierHeld.
  -->
  <trustInfo xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
    <security>
      <requestedPrivileges>
        <requestedExecutionLevel level="requireAdministrator" uiAccess="false" />
      </requestedPrivileges>
    </security>
  </trustInfo>
</assembly>
